ass at most two; then check every step claiming exp(K) divides p, including normal generation, central generator commutators, and arbitrary products. Also check the integral Hall-coordinate formula and the isolation of the unique multidegree (p,1) term in G/K. Kill immediately if the terminal exponent lemma is circular or incomplete. If the lemma survives, prepare a partial-result claim and constraint matrix for Validator, then use only the remaining block to identify—not hand-wave—the first class-p-plus-two obstruction.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
