atisfying all remaining admissibility rows.\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"source_clause_id\": \"c-odd\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"constraint_id\": \"21.137-odd-p-not-2\",\n      \"kind\": \"exclusion\",\n      \"role\": \"admissibility\",\n      \"statement\": \"p is prime and p is not 2; equivalently p>2.\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"source_clause_id\": \"c-odd\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"constraint_id\": \"21.137-odd-finite-p-group\",\n      \"kind\": \"object_class\",\n      \"role\": \"admissibility\",\n      \"statement\": \"G is a finite p-group for that same odd prime p.\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"source_clause_id\": \"c-odd\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"constraint_id\": \"21.137-odd-exponent-p2\",\n      \"kind\": \"exponent\",\n      \"role\": \"admissibility\",\n      \"statement\": \"The exponent of G is exactly p^2.\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"source_clause_id\": \"c-odd\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"constraint_id\": \"21.137-odd-power-set-definition\",\n      \"kind\": \"definition\",\n      \"role\": \"admissibility\",\n      \"statement\": \"P is the set of all actual p-th powers {g^p : g in G}, not merely the subgroup generated by those powers.\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"source_clause_id\": \"c-odd\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"constraint_id\": \"21.137-odd-power-set-subgroup\",\n      \"kind\": \"hypothesis\",\n      \"role\": \"admissibility\",\n      \"statement\": \"The set P of actual p-th powers is closed as a subgroup of G.\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"source_clause_id\": \"c-odd\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"constraint_id\": \"21.137-odd-P-abelian\",\n      \"kind\": \"conclusion\",\n      \"role\": \"target_conclusion\",\n      \"statement\": \"P is abelian.\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"source_clause_id\": \"c-odd\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"excluded_scopes\": [\n    \"21.137/two-group-exponent-8\",\n    \"Any p=2 example\",\n    \"Any odd-prime group whose exponent is not exactly p^2\"\n  ],\n  \"success_criteria\": {\n    \"proof\": \"Prove P abelian for every odd prime p and every finite p-group G of exponent exactly p^2 whose actual p-th-power set P is a subgroup.\",\n    \"counterexample\": \"Give a reconstructible finite p-group for an explicitly odd prime p, of exponent exactly p^2, whose actual p-th-power set is a subgroup but is nonabelian.\",\n    \"partial_progress\": [\n      \"A proved reduction from closure of the p-th-power set to explicit commutator identities.\",\n      \"A complete, reproducible exclusion or construction result for a structurally defined family at an odd prime.\"\n    ],\n    \"certificate\": \"A line-by-line proof, or a presentation and independent checks of p>2, exact exponent p^2, equality with the actual power set, subgroup closure, and nonabelianity.\"\n  },\n  \"selection_status\": \"active\",\n  \"state\": \"awaiting_lead\",\n  \"scope_answered\": false,\n  \"active_direction\": \"counterexample\",\n  \"truth_likelihood\": {\n    \"estimate\": 0.5,\n    \"rationale\": \"The proof direction produced strong necessary conditions but its affine/Hall/action mechanism admits sharp nonabelian action models; a fresh counterexample construction is now competitive. This remains a planning estimate only.\",\n    \"updated_utc\": \"2026-08-16T12:57:21Z\"\n  },\n  \"priority\": {\n    \"importance\": 4,\n    \"probability_of_substantial_progress\": 0.4,\n    \"verifiability\": 5,\n    \"expected_active_hours\": 3.0,\n    \"rationale\": \"The clause is exact, parameter-sensitive, and supports both algebraic reductions and independently checkable finite models.\"\n  },\n  \"direction_sessions\": {\n    \"proof\": {\n      \"session_id\": \"01a00a68-c5c9-7f53-b31a-0cfdc7e0d4a2\",\n      \"state\": \"complete\",\n      \"parent_session_id\": \"01a00064-840f-7150-b101-e01ea04d1660\",\n      \"fresh_session_reason\": \"The old session was anchored to an excluded p=2 clause and solution-bearing context; the human requested a blind odd-prime restart.\"\n    },\n    \"counterexample\": {\n      \"session_id\": \"01a00ab7-4414-7342-a557-01e6ae19bfce\",\n      \"state\": \"complete\",\n      \"parent_session_id\": \"01a00a68-c5c9-7f53-b31a-0cfdc7e0d4a2\",\n      \"fresh_session_reason\": \"The proof-direction affine/Hall/action representation met its explicit kill criterion after 64 active minutes; the independent alternate direction now uses a curated reviewed handoff.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"current_strategy\": \"human-priority one-hour pivot after the minimal p=3 ansatz failed; clean MathExpert comparing a non-wreath construction with return to proof\",\n  \"strategy_history\": [\n    \"The legacy p=2 direction is excluded from this scope and from the clean-context prompt.\",\n    \"The direct minimal p=3 ansatz was killed at 90 cumulative minutes: split models had abelian cubes or a zero-fibre closure defect, and the next coefficient family violated the reviewed |P|>=3^5 gate before computation.\",\n    \"Human priority window from 2026-08-16T13:45:05Z: devote the next hour to 21.137; forbid wreath-shaped routes because of filename-only prior exposure and obtain a clean MathExpert pivot before the next major branch.\"\n  ],\n  \"latest_outcome\": \"Counterexample minimal ansatz exhausted with no admissible candidate; one-hour human-priority pivot and clean MathExpert consultation active\",\n  \"open_questions\": [],\n  \"revision_history\": [\n    {\n      \"revision\": 1,\n      \"changed_utc\": \"2026-08-14T13:09:58Z\",\n      \"reason\": \"Legacy whole-problem assignment; no canonical atomic record existed.\",\n      \"supersedes\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"revision\": 2,\n      \"changed_utc\": \"2026-08-16T11:13:07Z\",\n      \"reason\": \"Atomize the odd-prime exponent-p^2 clause and exclude the separate exponent-8 two-group clause.\",\n      \"supersedes\": [\n        \"legacy whole-problem assignment\",\n        \"all revision-1 control messages\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"blind_run\": {\n